<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Fire2MQTT is a LAN-only sideloaded app for Fire TV. It makes exactly
    one network call: MQTT to a user-configured broker (typically Mosquitto
    on the same home subnet, port 1883).

    Why a process-wide cleartext allow rather than a narrow allowlist:
    - Android network_security_config <domain> entries are literal hostname
      or IP matches; there is no syntax for an IPv4 subnet range
      (e.g. 192.168.0.0/16). The broker host is only known at runtime, so
      an install-time allowlist cannot cover the user's LAN.
    - The app has no other outbound network paths; INTERNET is held purely
      for MQTT. There are no analytics, no remote config, no crash
      reporters, no HTTP clients.
    - TLS to a home MQTT broker is out of scope for v1 (most default
      Mosquitto installs are not TLS-configured).

    A future revision that adds outbound HTTP for anything else MUST
    revisit this policy.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
